WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.216
A task comes to mind while you are writing
an e-mail or reading a web page.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.566
Switching to a browser tab and finding the
right list breaks your flow.

00:00:09.866 --> 00:00:11.828
With Merkzettel, it takes one shortcut.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.382
Press Meta, Alt and N in any application.

00:00:18.682 --> 00:00:22.118
Merkzettel comes to the front, with the
cursor in the new task field.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:27.550
Type the task.

00:00:27.602 --> 00:00:32.214
A date word at the end sets the due date:
tomorrow, a weekday, or a date like the

00:00:32.264 --> 00:00:33.464
25th of May.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.343
Press Enter.

00:00:38.393 --> 00:00:41.818
The date word disappears from the title,
and the task is due tomorrow.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.589
Weekdays work the same way: this task is
due on Friday.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.579
Close the window, and you are back where
you left off.

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:58.085
Merkzettel keeps running in the system
tray.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:05.647
Let Merkzettel start with your session,
and the shortcut is always ready.

00:01:05.947 --> 00:01:07.863
You can change it in the system settings.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.347
That is how you capture tasks from
anywhere.

